  "slug": "nowhere-boy-screening-abbey-road-studios",
  "title": "Nowhere Boy screening at Studio Two, Abbey Road Studios",
  "date": "2009-11-30",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>A special screening of <a href=\"/film-and-video/nowhere-boy/\"><em>Nowhere Boy</em></a>, the biopic of <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>’s teenage years, was held at the famous Studio Two at <a href=\"/features/abbey-road-studios/\">Abbey Road Studios</a> on 30 November 2009. <span id=\"more-3392\"></span></p><p><a href=\"/gallery/miscellany/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_01/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-8768\"><img decoding=\"sync\" data-attachment-id=\"8768\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/miscellany/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1504,1000\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"Abbey Road Studios, 30 November 2009\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_01-960x638.jpg\" src=\"/wp/media/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_01-200x132.jpg\" alt=\"Abbey Road Studios, 30 November 2009\" title=\"Abbey Road Studios, 30 November 2009\" width=\"200\" height=\"132\" class=\"alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-8768\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a>The screening was held by Sony for special guests and members of the press, including The Beatles Bible. The film was introduced by director Sam Taylor-Wood, who attended with her fiancé Aaron Johnson. Other guests included Martha and Rufus Wainwright.</p><p>It’s hard not to feel a sense of excitement when entering Studio Two. After all, this is the sacred space where around four fifths of The Beatles’ music was recorded, from <a href=\"/songs/love-me-do/\">‘Love Me Do’</a> through to <a href=\"/albums/let-it-be/\"><em>Let It Be</em></a>. Its interior is famous from photographs of the group at work, and on the surface it remains largely unchanged since the 1960s.</p><p>Studio Two is in the basement of Abbey Road Studios. Along the right hand side runs the flight of stairs to the control room, where <a href=\"/people/george-martin/\">George Martin</a> and the incomparable studio engineers used to observe and record The Beatles at work. At the foot of the stairs was a Steinway grand piano.</p><p><a href=\"/gallery/miscellany/2009_nowhere-boy-in-spite-of-all-the-danger/\" rel=\"attachment wp-att-8561\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxOTUiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTk1IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" data-attachment-id=\"8561\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/miscellany/2009_nowhere-boy-in-spite-of-all-the-danger/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/2009_nowhere-boy-in-spite-of-all-the-danger.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1000,1021\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"In Spite Of All The Danger promotional single for Nowhere Boy (2009)\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/2009_nowhere-boy-in-spite-of-all-the-danger-940x960.jpg\" data-src=\"/wp/media/2009_nowhere-boy-in-spite-of-all-the-danger-195x200.jpg\" alt=\"In Spite Of All The Danger promotional single for Nowhere Boy (2009)\" title=\"In Spite Of All The Danger promotional single for Nowhere Boy (2009)\" width=\"195\" height=\"200\" class=\"alignright size-thumbnail wp-image-8561\"></a>A temporary cinema screen was erected on the studio floor. Chairs laid out for the guests, on each of which was placed a promotional 7″ single of The Nowhere Boys – the actors who played the Quarrymen/Beatles in the film – performing <a href=\"/songs/thatll-be-the-day/\">‘That’ll Be The Day’</a> and <a href=\"/songs/in-spite-of-all-the-danger/\">‘In Spite Of All The Danger’</a>. The two songs were recorded by the Quarrymen in 1958 in a Liverpool home studio, a scene recreated in Nowhere Boy.</p><p>I was early for the screening. While the other guests were guided to the canteen I was allowed to take photographs of the studio, though sadly not the control room, while the technicians finalised testing the sound and visuals.</p><p>Before the screening began, Sam Taylor-Wood spoke briefly to the guests. Although evidently nervous at having to address a crowd, she joked about worrying that the studio acoustics wouldn’t do the film justice, and spoke about the journey she’d embarked upon coming to a fitting end at Abbey Road, and about rock ‘n’ roll coming home to its spiritual home. Aaron Johnson kept a low-key presence at the back of the room.</p><p>Read our <a href=\"/film-and-video/nowhere-boy/\">review of the film</a>, and feature on the <a href=\"/albums/nowhere-boy-original-soundtrack/\">soundtrack album</a>.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/2009/11/30/nowhere-boy-screening-abbey-road-studios/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-3392 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon landscape\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/miscellany/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_02/\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIyMDAiIGhlaWdodD0iMTMzIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMjAwIDEzMyI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"133\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_02-200x133.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"Nowhere Boy screening at Studio Two, Abbey Road Studios, 30 November 2009\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/091130_nowhere-boy-abbey-road_02-200x133.jpg 200w, 